{:ev/id "lc-0023" :ev/ns "loretile-code" :ev/actor "build.py" :ev/ts 1792000000022 :ev/type :concept-accepted :concept {:id "m-exercise" :title "loretile.exercise" :definition "Items whose answer is EXECUTED (wiki/Exercises.md) — for any subject that has code in it, not one language. An exercise names its RUNTIME and its CHECK; the card, the attempt log and the author's gate are the same for… (src/loretile/exercise.cljs)" :kind :module :source-id "src-exercise"}}
{:ev/id "lc-0024" :ev/ns "loretile-code" :ev/actor "build.py" :ev/ts 1792000000023 :ev/type :object-added :object {:id "o-m-exercise" :concept-id "m-exercise" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Items whose answer is EXECUTED (wiki/Exercises.md) — for any subject that has code in it, not one language. An exercise names its RUNTIME and its CHECK; the card, the attempt log and the author's gate are the same for every pair. Runtimes (kernel-shaped: execute code, get output or an error): - :pglite — real Postgres in WebAssembly, lazy-loaded from js/pglite/. ONE database per setup, ONE transaction per execution, rolled back. - :python — Pyodide in a worker (js/pyrunner.js + js/pyodide/), a FRESH namespace per execution, a timeout that terminates the worker. Further languages slot in here; R, C++ and the other xeus kernels need their environments built first (wiki «browser kernels»). Checks — deterministic and ours, never the engine's: - :rows (SQL) the learner's rows = the solution's rows - :output the learner's printed output (+ last value) = the solution's - :assert hidden checks run after the learner's code; passing = no error Absent fields mean the first exercises' shape: :pglite with :rows." :grounded-in "src-exercise"}}
