{:ev/id "lc-0068" :ev/ns "loretile-code" :ev/actor "build.py" :ev/ts 1792000000067 :ev/type :concept-accepted :concept {:id "m-session" :title "loretile.session" :definition "The assistant's conversations, kept across reloads (kintale.session, Denis 2026-09-08: «adopt sessions from kintale»). The whole sitting is kept — bubbles, open cards, the pending attachment — because a curator who… (src/loretile/session.cljs)" :kind :module :source-id "src-session"}}
{:ev/id "lc-0069" :ev/ns "loretile-code" :ev/actor "build.py" :ev/ts 1792000000068 :ev/type :object-added :object {:id "o-m-session" :concept-id "m-session" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "The assistant's conversations, kept across reloads (kintale.session, Denis 2026-09-08: «adopt sessions from kintale»). The whole sitting is kept — bubbles, open cards, the pending attachment — because a curator who comes back to cards without the talk has lost the thread. Plain localStorage, no vault: org knowledge, not family secrets (wiki/Architecture.md — no E2E here). Per DEVICE, never synced: a conversation is a workbench, the event log is what is shared. BOUNDED: the visible history and the shelf of past sittings are capped; an attachment's text (up to 100k chars) is dropped when a sitting is shelved — it only mattered until it was sent." :grounded-in "src-session"}}
