{:ev/id "lc-0077" :ev/ns "loretile-code" :ev/actor "build.py" :ev/ts 1792000000076 :ev/type :concept-accepted :concept {:id "m-tools" :title "loretile.tools" :definition "The tool registry — the assistant's hands (wiki/Assistant.md, the kintale.tools shape). A tool is ONE map {:name :doc :args :confirm :handler}; everything the model and the chat need — the prompt block, the dispatcher —… (src/loretile/tools.cljs)" :kind :module :source-id "src-tools"}}
{:ev/id "lc-0078" :ev/ns "loretile-code" :ev/actor "build.py" :ev/ts 1792000000077 :ev/type :object-added :object {:id "o-m-tools" :concept-id "m-tools" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "The tool registry — the assistant's hands (wiki/Assistant.md, the kintale.tools shape). A tool is ONE map {:name :doc :args :confirm :handler}; everything the model and the chat need — the prompt block, the dispatcher — is DERIVED from the registry, so adding a tool is adding one map, never edits across prompt and chat. Confirm classes keep the covenant «nothing lands unreviewed»: :auto — pure reads: run immediately, the result goes back to the model in a bounded look-don't-touch loop :card — writes: the ordinary proposal cards (the intake's own JSON) :action — moves or runs something, behind a one-tap card: the model proposes it in \"actions\", the user taps, only then it runs Calls are our own JSON in the reply ({\"tools\": [{\"name\" …}]}), not a provider's native tool calling — so every provider, Yandex and DeepSeek included, gets the same hands. Handlers are (fn [ctx args] -> string): ctx {:kg :graph-id}; the string is what the model reads. Tool definitions live in loretile.tool-defs, loaded at boot (they need the learner loop, which needs the chat)." :grounded-in "src-tools"}}
